    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, headlined by **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Trea Turner** is our clear priority play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Poulin\u2019s 4.96 xERA and a primary leadoff role that maximizes his league-leading stolen base potential. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is an elite start; while facing a respectable arm in Senga, his dynamic platoon advantage and top-of-the-order positioning make him a focal point. **Caleb Durbin** also enters the fray as a high-value play (70.67), largely driven by the extremely favorable matchup against Sullivan\u2019s 6.74 xERA, which provides a massive ceiling for total bases and potential SB opportunities despite the volatility of the pitcher\u2019s profile.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult exclusion today was **Chase Meidroth** (45.03), who was the first player left off the active roster. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a baseline that flirted with marginal territory, his inefficiency against a tougher pitcher in Messick (3.55 xERA) relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-ceiling options like **Nelson Velazquez** (58.75), whose elite xwOBA of 0.421 provides more reliable offensive production in the mid-tier. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Lars Nootbaar** (49.71); despite his placement in the lineup, his negative platoon split against Rodriguez creates a risk that could drag down our batting average floor, making him a candidate to be swapped if official lineups shift. We are currently navigating these decisions without **Kyle Schwarber**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Hyeseong Kim**, all of whom are unavailable due to rest or minor league assignment, further tightening our depth for this critical 5x5 rotation.",
